ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: red
PROMPT_VERSION: v001
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "Hugging Face Transformers / LayerSkip", url: "https://huggingface.co/blog/layerskip", overlap: "Implements early-exit self-speculative decoding via `assistant_early_exit`; overlaps with token/layer early exit, but not agentic token-class thresholds."},
  {system: "SGLang", url: "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sgl-project/sglang/main/docs/advanced_features/speculative_decoding.md", overlap: "Ships EAGLE-2/EAGLE-3, MTP, standalone draft-model, and NGRAM speculative decoding; also adaptive speculative decoding by accept length, not schema/boilerplate class."},
  {system: "vLLM", url: "https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/features/speculative_decoding/", overlap: "Ships speculative decoding infrastructure including draft-model/EAGLE/MTP/N-gram families; overlap is inference acceleration, not confidence early-exit per token class."},
  {system: "TensorRT-LLM", url: "https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/advanced/speculative-decoding.html", overlap: "Ships speculative sampling with draft-target, NGram, Medusa, ReDrafter, EAGLE, and Lookahead; no evidence of structure-aware early-exit thresholds."},
  {system: "FlashInfer", url: "https://flashinfer.ai/2024/02/02/introduce-flashinfer.html", overlap: "Kernel library for LLM serving attention/KV-cache performance; no early-exit policy overlap."},
  {system: "LMCache", url: "https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache", overlap: "KV-cache reuse/offload layer for serving; no early-exit policy overlap."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight
SCALE_REALISM: Does not hold as a systems claim yet. Evidence is an L0 analytic CPU/std-lib model, not a real LM/server/GPU artifact. The submitted structure-aware mechanism is negative: +0.46pp FLOPs at realistic f, 0/90 configurations above the 5pp bar. The surviving agentic>reasoning observation is only modeled and is already delivered by a tuned global threshold; real wall-clock, batching raggedness, intermediate-head overhead, KV-cache effects, and sequence-level tool-call quality are unmeasured.
RATIONALE: Early-exit itself is prior art: CALM (https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.07061), Depth-Adaptive Transformer (https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.10073), SkipDecode (https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.02628), and LayerSkip (https://aclanthology.org/2024.acl-long.681/). Shipping systems already cover adjacent inference mechanisms: Transformers/LayerSkip exposes early-exit self-speculative generation; SGLang, vLLM, and TensorRT-LLM ship speculative decoding variants. I found no shipping system doing the exact schema/boilerplate-conditioned threshold, but the packet’s own tuned-global baseline kills that mechanism at realistic f. This is not a systems design contribution; at best it is a negative analytic insight requiring real trace measurement and GPU/server validation before map promotion.
